# Cloudflare Pages redirects / rewrites.
#
# This file is copied verbatim from static/ into public/_redirects by Zola.
# Cloudflare Pages consumes it at deploy time.
#
# The rule below is ONLY needed if the Worker is deployed on a separate
# subdomain (e.g. api.swimfrancisco.com) AND Pages is NOT configured with a
# same-origin route like swimfrancisco.com/api/*. It rewrites same-origin
# /api/* requests to the Worker so the browser never makes a cross-origin
# call (status 200 = rewrite/proxy, not a visible 3xx redirect).
#
# If the Worker is bound to swimfrancisco.com/api/* directly via a Workers
# route (recommended — see docs/deploy.md option C), this rule is a harmless
# no-op because the Worker route wins before Pages serves anything.
#
# Uncomment once api.swimfrancisco.com is live:
# /api/*  https://api.swimfrancisco.com/api/:splat  200
